# Accessibility (a11y) Best Practices

**WCAG 2.1 AA** — semantic HTML first, ARIA only when needed; visible `focus-visible` states using token rings (`ring-ring`, `ring-offset-background`).

## Enforced (deterministic)

Mechanically enforced via `check:a11y-structure` and `check:a11y-contrast` — see AGENTS.md § Hard constraints:

### Structure (`check:a11y-structure`)

- **One `<h1>` per route** — each `page.tsx` / `error.tsx` surface, its segment `layout.tsx` chain, and import closure must contain exactly one semantic h1.
- **Non-empty `alt` on meaningful images** — same scan scope as h1; decorative images may use empty `alt` when marked with `role="presentation"` or `aria-hidden`. Dynamic `alt={expr}` is call-site responsibility (static-analysis ceiling — see `scripts/checks/a11y-structure.mjs` `// debt:` markers).
- **No skipped heading levels** — in the route entry JSX tree and its import closure, document-order headings must not jump more than one level (e.g. h1 → h3). Segment `layout.tsx` headings are excluded (static-analysis ceiling — see checker `// debt:` markers).

### Color contrast (`check:a11y-contrast`)

Paired semantic token foregrounds in `src/app/globals.css` (`:root` and `.dark`) must meet **WCAG AA 4.5:1** — the checker owns the pair inventory. Chart, border, ring, and input tokens are out of scope (no foreground partner). Token parsing ceilings (var() indirection, alpha compositing) — see `scripts/checks/a11y-contrast.mjs` `// debt:` markers.

## Guidance (manual / subjective)

Screen-reader UX and keyboard flows stay manual review — the items below are not covered by `check:*`.

## Tooltips

**Default: no tooltip.** Add one only when:
- **(a) Icon-only control whose function isn't inferable** from the icon/label alone, or
- **(b) State-dependent behavior** needs explaining (why a control is disabled, what a toggle's on/off state actually does).

Don't tooltip a control just because a sibling control has one — symmetry isn't a reason on its own.

**Delay & motion:** 500ms hover delay, fade-in. No instant (0ms) tooltips outside the collapsed sidebar nav (`SidebarMenuButton`), which is a distinct, deliberate pattern for icon-only nav wayfinding.

**Copy tone:** short imperative for action controls ("Filter to debug logs"); one-line explanatory only when covering a state/consequence a label can't ("Feed paused — Refresh to catch up").

**ARIA:** pick one relationship per control, don't mix — either the tooltip text *is* the `aria-label` (icon-only controls with no other visible text), or the tooltip *supplements* a separately-set `aria-label`/visible label. Don't duplicate near-identical text across both mechanisms on the same control.

## shadcn/ui + Radix
shadcn/ui components have **built-in accessibility** via Radix UI (ARIA, keyboard navigation, focus management, screen reader support). When customizing shadcn components, preserve Radix accessibility props — do not override ARIA roles or strip keyboard handlers.

## Principles
- **Semantic HTML first** — use native elements (`button`, `a`, `nav`, `main`) before synthetic roles
- **ARIA** — add only when semantic HTML is insufficient (icon-only buttons, complex widgets)
- **Keyboard** — all interactive elements operable without a mouse; prefer native elements over `div` + `role="button"`
- **Focus** — visible `focus-visible` rings using semantic tokens; never remove focus indicators
- **Forms** — associate labels, describe errors accessibly (`role="alert"`), use `aria-invalid` where appropriate
- **Modals** — use shadcn Dialog (focus trap, Escape to close, focus restore built-in)

## Manual review checklist
- [ ] Keyboard-only path reaches every interactive control (Tab / Shift+Tab / Enter / Space / Escape)
- [ ] Screen reader announces control purpose and state changes (icon-only buttons, live regions, dialogs)
- [ ] Form errors are announced (`role="alert"` / `aria-invalid`) without relying on color alone
